  "worked_solution": "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=30$ and ${S}_{N}=1\\,080$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =\\frac{30}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(30-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =15(2{a}_{1}+29d) \\\\ \\frac{1\\,080}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $17$th term of the arithmetic series  and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{17} & ={a}_{1}+(17-1)d \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}+16d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}33={a}_{1}+16d \\\\ 72=2{a}_{1}+29d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-66 & =-2{a}_{1}-32d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 6 & =-3d \\\\ d & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33 & ={a}_{1}+16(-2) \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}-32 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
